# Single source of truth for the we-are-mono/ASK commit used by the OOT
# kernel modules (cdx.ko, fci.ko, auto_bridge.ko) and userspace daemons
# (cmm, dpa_app). Sourced by bin/ci-build-ask-modules.sh and
# bin/ci-build-ask-userspace.sh -- bump ASK_VERSION here only, never in
# either script directly, so the two builds can never disagree.
#
# NOTE (2026-09-11): this does NOT yet cover kernel/flavors/ask/patches/
# 010-098. Those were vendored from we-are-mono/ASK's `fix/security-
# hardening` branch, which has since been deleted upstream -- the
# individual commit SHAs embedded in each patch's own `From <sha>` header
# (e.g. 010-ask-fman-dpaa-ehash.patch -> e2b08ea9...) are now dangling
# (confirmed: `git fetch <sha>` fails with "not our ref"). There is
# currently no live upstream ref the kernel patches can be re-verified or
# re-diffed against. See plans/enumerated-forging-pie.md (Phase 2) for the
# fix: resync kernel patches + this pin together onto one live ASK commit,
# with a scratch-repo + hardware validation pass before landing.
ASK_REPO=https://github.com/we-are-mono/ASK.git
ASK_VERSION=a211ea865379362058c6656b9c448e4a7050e93c
